## Phase 2 - Host the relay

*Day 1-2 - required for real users*

The app is useless on phones without a public relay. Right now it defaults to `localhost`.

### Option A - Easiest (Railway / Render / Fly.io)

1. Create an account on [Railway](https://railway.app), [Render](https://render.com), or [Fly.io](https://fly.io).
2. Deploy `sentinel/server/` (Node app, port 8787, needs persistent disk for `data/`).
3. Enable HTTPS so your URL becomes `wss://your-relay.up.railway.app` (or similar).
4. Test:
```bash
   curl https://your-relay-url/   # should say: Sentinel relay up
```

### Option B - More control (VPS, ~$5/mo)

Hetzner / DigitalOcean -> install Node -> run `node relay.js` -> put Caddy/nginx in front for TLS.

### Option C - Max privacy story (later)

Tor onion via `sentinel/server/onion/` - good for v2, not required for first launch.

**Done when:** you have a working `wss://...` URL that stays up 24/7.

**Cost:** ~$0-7/month.

