## Phase 6 - Google Play Store prep

*Week 2-3*

### 6.1 Accounts & money

| Item | Cost |
|------|------|
| Google Play Developer | **$25 one-time** -> [play.google.com/console](https://play.google.com/console) |
| Expo (builds) | Free tier -> paid if you scale |

### 6.2 Store assets (prepare before upload)

- **App icon** - you have `sentinel/assets/icon.png` (1024x1024)
- **Screenshots** - 2-8 phone screenshots (chat list, chat, profile, channels)
- **Short description** (~80 chars)
- **Full description** - privacy, E2EE, no phone number
- **Privacy policy URL** - required (add a page on your Vercel site)
- **Support email** - required

### 6.3 Play Console forms

1. **Data safety** - declare: username, password (hashed on server), messages (E2EE ciphertext), optional avatar.
2. **Content rating** - questionnaire (likely low maturity for a chat app).
3. **Encryption export** - `ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption: false` is already in `app.json` for iOS; Android has similar declarations in Play Console.
4. **Target audience** - age group, etc.

### 6.4 Production Android build

```bash
cd sentinel
EXPO_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL="wss://YOUR-RELAY-URL" \
  eas build -p android --profile production
```

This produces an **`.aab`** (App Bundle), not APK - required for the Play Store.

### 6.5 Upload

```bash
eas submit -p android
```

Or upload the `.aab` manually in Play Console.

### 6.6 Release track (recommended order)

1. **Internal testing** - up to 100 testers, fastest, minimal review
2. **Closed testing** - larger group, still not public
3. **Open testing** - optional public beta
4. **Production** - full public listing (Google review, often 3-7 days first time)

**Done when:** app is installable from Play Store (at least internal track).

